WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:08.780
Excuse me, miss.

2
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.730
I've received a call about loitering.

3
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.169
There's no one here, idiot.

4
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.080
Oh, yeah.

5
00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:16.060
What's up?

6
00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:17.339
I need information.

7
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.649
Who had Big Joe nicked?

8
00:00:19.739 --> 00:00:21.739
Arresting officer was George Brightwell,

9
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:22.559
I think.

10
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.899
No, I'm sure.

11
00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:26.739
Danny, you forgetting you owe me a grand?

12
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.460
I'm not talking about the arresting officer.

13
00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:33.149
I'm saying who made the call?

14
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.840
I'm not totally sure about this,

15
00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:40.949
but I think it's Callum Miller.

16
00:00:41.179 --> 00:00:42.479
Detective Sergeant, right?

17
00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:44.640
What do you know about him?

18
00:00:45.119 --> 00:00:47.119
He's Michael Eversholt's crony in chief.

19
00:00:47.659 --> 00:00:49.109
Beyond that, I'd be guessing.

20
00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:52.039
But I know someone who knows more.

21
00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:54.740
You need to talk to Curtis Watson,

22
00:00:55.079 --> 00:00:56.079
detective Constable.

23
00:00:56.539 --> 00:00:57.500
Hates Miller.

24
00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.740
I don't blame him. Give me his details.

25
00:01:02.439 --> 00:01:04.459
You may be looking at the crews and

26
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.299
thinking we're the dominant power

27
00:01:07.079 --> 00:01:08.079
in Croydon.

28
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.620
In reality, we're small fry.

29
00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:14.039
Top of the food chain in the borough

30
00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:17.870
is Croydon East MP Stuart Jordan,

31
00:01:18.219 --> 00:01:20.990
a corrupt piece of shit who views

32
00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.380
the borough treasury as his

33
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:24.080
personal

34
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.180
piggy bank.

35
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.400
And just further down is Police Borough

36
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.019
Commander Michael Eversholt.

37
00:01:35.239 --> 00:01:36.239
You Watson?

38
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.560
Call me Curtis.

39
00:01:38.379 --> 00:01:39.530
You know Callum Miller?

40
00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:41.019
Bit of a history lesson.

41
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.900
Michael Eversholt gets transferred

42
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.359
from Eltham to

43
00:01:46.459 --> 00:01:48.900
Croton in nineteen

44
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.000
ninety-nine

45
00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.400
in the wake of the Stephen Lawrence inquiry.

46
00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.140
Institutional racism.

47
00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.680
And for all we can tell,

48
00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.440
he's got no plans to improve once he

49
00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.890
gets to Croton.

50
00:01:58.989 --> 00:02:00.589
Then he makes borough commander,

51
00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.920
and everything gets worse.

52
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:05.940
Then a few months back,

53
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.040
I make a mistake.

54
00:02:08.139 --> 00:02:09.389
I start asking questions.

55
00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.960
Questions like why it took me twice

56
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.360
as long to make detective.

57
00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:16.719
Why one of the black PCs found a banana

58
00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:17.819
in his locker.

59
00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.310
Eversholt doesn't go after me directly.

60
00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:21.719
He uses his lackey, Miller,

61
00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:23.960
to drive me out. Bogus leads,

62
00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.430
interviews with dead-end witnesses.

63
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:27.360
Even now

64
00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.840
I'm working on a case of a few dead cats

65
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.500
that everyone knows are just foxes.

66
00:02:37.919 --> 00:02:39.379
Do you know why Miller wanted Big Joe

67
00:02:39.479 --> 00:02:40.479
Adebayor?

68
00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.080
To go down?

69
00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:46.500
No. But if we find out why,

70
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.700
we can push for a malicious prosecution

71
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.620
angle.

72
00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.639
Your boy goes free,

73
00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:58.280
and Miller is left red-faced.

74
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.120
Where do I start?

75
00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:05.240
He's got a safe in his office he puts

76
00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.990
the most sensitive case files in.

77
00:03:07.759 --> 00:03:09.109
The truth will be in there.

78
00:03:09.479 --> 00:03:11.340
I made a copy of the key a while back.

79
00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:13.919
I wanted to nail him. This might be it.

80
00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:16.580
I can give you a five-minute window,

81
00:03:17.599 --> 00:03:18.400
but if you get caught,

82
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.500
your life is over.

83
00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:22.460
You wanna nominate someone for this?

84
00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.759
Nah. Handle this myself in it
